WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.460
How do you map which neurons connect inside a tangled brain?

2
00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:10.300
A neuron's long output fibre, its axon, travels inside bundles called tracts.

3
00:00:11.660 --> 00:00:16.280
Because a neuron carries no label showing its partners, that wiring stays hidden.

4
00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:24.590
Neurons already move cargo along axons using their own transport machinery.

5
00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:28.830
Tract tracing puts visible dye onto that traffic.

6
00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:34.450
Inject biotinylated dextran amine near cell bodies in one region.

7
00:00:35.770 --> 00:00:38.390
Those neurons carry it forward toward their terminals.

8
00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:44.330
This forward mapping, called anterograde tracing, shows where those cells project.

9
00:00:45.483 --> 00:00:50.083
Axon transport also runs backward, from terminals to cell bodies.

10
00:00:51.443 --> 00:00:53.983
Inject Fluorogold into a target region instead.

11
00:00:55.483 --> 00:00:58.983
Terminals there absorb it and carry it back to distant cell bodies.

12
00:01:00.283 --> 00:01:02.763
That reverse route is retrograde tracing.

13
00:01:04.163 --> 00:01:09.043
Every tracer uses axon transport to turn hidden wiring into visible paths.

14
00:01:10.133 --> 00:01:11.493
Now test that logic.

15
00:01:12.973 --> 00:01:16.753
Cholera toxin B subunit travels both ways along an axon.

16
00:01:17.993 --> 00:01:22.333
Suppose you inject it into a middle region, and a neighbouring region glows.

17
00:01:23.593 --> 00:01:27.593
From that bright patch alone, can you tell whether axons enter or leave?

18
00:01:33.167 --> 00:01:34.567
Not from the glow alone.

19
00:01:35.767 --> 00:01:41.007
Because cholera toxin B subunit travels both ways, researchers must establish

20
00:01:41.007 --> 00:01:42.827
direction for each tracer first.

21
00:01:44.387 --> 00:01:46.227
Dye injections carry a second limit.

22
00:01:47.387 --> 00:01:50.147
They mark cells or terminals taking up enough dye.

23
00:01:51.307 --> 00:01:54.687
That reveals population wiring, not one cell's synapses.

24
00:01:55.900 --> 00:02:00.820
To pinpoint direct partners, researchers use genetically targeted viruses.

25
00:02:02.260 --> 00:02:07.640
A modified rabies virus starts in a defined starter population, or even one starter

26
00:02:07.640 --> 00:02:14.160
cell. Restricted to one synaptic step, it crosses one synapse back to label the

27
00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:15.600
neurons that feed it directly.

28
00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:19.520
Even one-step tracing has a strict limit.

29
00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:26.440
In mice, modified rabies virus linked gut lining cells to vagal sensory neurons.

30
00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:31.840
Labelling reached them in 2 of 5 mice with infected colon nerves.

31
00:02:32.980 --> 00:02:37.840
That shows a connection in some animals, not the transmitter or behavioural role.

32
00:02:38.883 --> 00:02:42.883
Paired with other tests, circuit mapping unlocked landmark pathways.

33
00:02:44.323 --> 00:02:50.743
In 1976, Fernando Nottebohm, Tegner Stokes and Christiana Leonard mapped the adult

34
00:02:50.743 --> 00:02:51.923
canary song circuit.

35
00:02:53.143 --> 00:02:57.023
Forebrain cluster HVC projects to a second cluster, RA.

36
00:02:58.323 --> 00:03:01.823
RA reaches brainstem motor neurons of the vocal organ.

37
00:03:02.883 --> 00:03:09.003
In 1989, Andrew Lumsden and Roger Keynes mapped cranial motor neurons in chick

38
00:03:09.003 --> 00:03:14.183
embryos. These neurons drive muscles of the jaw, face and throat.

39
00:03:15.663 --> 00:03:20.703
Mapping their origins showed each cranial nerve's motor neurons come from a pair of

40
00:03:20.703 --> 00:03:21.763
hindbrain segments.

41
00:03:22.783 --> 00:03:28.223
And David Hubel, Torsten Wiesel and Simon LeVay closed one eye in infant macaque

42
00:03:28.223 --> 00:03:34.283
monkeys. Tracing stripes in visual cortex showed the open eye's stripes widened

43
00:03:34.283 --> 00:03:36.043
while the closed eye's narrowed.

44
00:03:37.403 --> 00:03:42.663
Across brains, axon transport turns hidden wiring into maps that physiology can

45
00:03:42.663 --> 00:03:43.003
test.
